{
 "name": "low_traffic",
 "description": "CAUTION LOW (UAS airspace intrusion): a fresh airborne aircraft within 3 km of the observer or of a live drone and below 460 m above ground, one alert per aircraft, anchored on the observer within 3 km else on the nearest live drone; the ground is the one under the anchor: the anchor drone's alt_geo minus its height, else the observer's elevation, else the lowest live drone's alt_geo minus its height; height unknown is raised, never silent; aircraft on the ground never; a warning for the same aircraft supersedes its LOW; clears 20 s after it stops holding.",
 "worked_example": [
  "t=0: observer elevation 30 m is the ground. N911HC (0a1b2c) 1485 m E, 1485 m N of the observer at alt_geom 400 m: 2100.1 m, 370 m above ground < 460 -> anchored on the observer: 'LOW TRAFFIC NE 2.1 KM' / 'BE READY TO LAND DRONES; AIRCRAFT 370 M ABOVE GROUND, 2.1 KM NE'.",
  "N456 (2a3b4c) is 6.8 km from the observer but 1.8 km N of live drone D9A21: anchored on it, 270 m above ground -> 'LOW TRAFFIC N 1.8 KM' (drone_id 1581F20000D9A21).",
  "BARO1 (4a5b6c) reports only altb_ft 800 = 243.8 m -> about 213.8 m above ground -> 'LOW TRAFFIC S 1.2 KM, APPROX.' / 'BE READY TO LAND DRONES; AIRCRAFT ABOUT 214 M ABOVE GROUND, 1.2 KM S'.",
  "BARO0 (8a9b0c) reports only altb_ft 90 = 27.4 m, at or below the 30 m ground: 'LOW TRAFFIC SW 850 M, APPROX.' / 'BE READY TO LAND DRONES; AIRCRAFT NEAR GROUND LEVEL, 850 M SW' (near ground level already says it is approximate: no ABOUT).",
  "N123 at 600 m (570 m above ground), MID8 at 1,200 m and HIGH7 at 5000 m: not LOW. GND1 is on the ground 500 m away: never LOW. W1 is 300 m from D9A21 and 50 m above it -> TRAFFIC NEAR DRONE D9A21 (warning), which supersedes its LOW.",
  "RIDGE9 (9a0b1c) at alt_geom 700 m is 1.5 km N of D9A22, which flies at alt_geo 400 m, 50 m above its take-off: the ground under that anchor is 350 m, so RIDGE9 is 350 m above it -> 'BE READY TO LAND DRONES; AIRCRAFT 350 M ABOVE GROUND, 1.5 KM N' (drone_id 1581F20000D9A22); measured from the observer's 30 m it would read 670 m and be missed.",
  "Status: 'conflict watch on, low traffic, 1 ADS-B conflict, data 3 s old' ('low traffic' whenever a LOW alert shows, one or many; pairs are counted as 'ADS-B conflicts'; aircraft are never counted).",
  "t=1: observer elevation unknown -> the fallback ground is the lowest live drone's alt_geo minus height: D9A21 150 - 120 = 30 m (D9A22 is higher) -> the same alerts (RIDGE9 still uses its own anchor's 350 m).",
  "t=2: no observer elevation and no drone height -> ground unknown -> an airborne aircraft within 3 km is raised with HEIGHT UNKNOWN when its own height is unknown or below 3,500 m MSL (TRAFFIC_LOW_UNKNOWN_GROUND_MAX_M): MID8 at 1,200 m -> 'BE READY TO LAND DRONES; AIRCRAFT HEIGHT UNKNOWN, 2.0 KM E', N123 at 600 m too; HIGH7 at 5,000 m cannot be within 460 m of any ground below 3,000 m -> nothing.",
  "t=3: elevation back but D9A22 reports no height -> RIDGE9 falls back to the observer's 30 m: 670 m above -> not LOW, held from t=3 (out of hold); at t=10 D9A22's height is back and it is raised again.",
  "t=10: elevation back; N911HC climbed to 700 m (670 m above ground) and N123/MID8 are above 460 m again -> held; t=30 (20 s later) cleared."
 ],
